@lang en
IMPORT `msig-cgl-special`

-- COMPREHENSIVE GENERAL LIABILITY INSURANCE COVERAGE PART (src:319-549): I the insuring
-- agreement and its exclusions (a)-(q), II Persons Insured, III Limits of Liability as
-- printed, IV Policy Territory. Each exclusion is one rule that answers "does it apply";
-- msig-cgl-answer.l4 asks them in order.
--
-- Two Special Conditions bear on this part and are encoded with the Special Conditions
-- (msig-cgl-special.l4): the Completed Operations Hazard and Products Hazard Exclusion
-- Clause, which removes from this part everything the products and completed operations
-- hazards contain, and the Combined Single Limit Endorsement, which rewrites III.

§ `COMPREHENSIVE GENERAL LIABILITY INSURANCE COVERAGE PART`
-- src:319 | COMPREHENSIVE GENERAL LIABILITY INSURANCE COVERAGE PART

§§ `I. COVERAGE A – BODILY INJURY LIABILITY; COVERAGE B – PROPERTY DAMAGE LIABILITY`

-- Three limbs a claim must meet: damages the insured is legally obligated to pay; because
-- of bodily injury or property damage as defined (which dates the harm inside the policy
-- period); caused by an occurrence. "to which this insurance applies" is the exclusions,
-- Persons Insured and IV, asked separately. The right and duty to defend and the end of
-- both on exhaustion of the limit are read in msig-cgl-answer.l4.
-- src:321 | l. COVERAGE A – BODILY INJURY LIABILITY
-- src:323 | COVERAGE B – PROPERTY DAMAGE LIABILITY
-- src:325 | The Company will pay on behalf of the insured all sums which the insured shall become legally obligated to pay as damages
-- src:326 | because of
-- src:328 | A - bodily injury or
-- src:330 | B - property damage
-- src:332 | to which this insurance applies, caused by an occurrence, and the Company shall have the right and duty to defend any suit
-- src:333 | against the insured seeking damages on account of such bodily injury or property damage, even if any of the allegations of the
-- src:334 | suit are groundless, false or fraudulent, and may make such investigation and settlement of any claim or suit as it deems
-- src:335 | expedient, but the Company shall not be obligated to pay any claim or judgement or to defend any suit after the applicable
-- src:336 | limit of the Company's liability has been exhausted by payment of judgements or settlements.
@ref src:325-332
GIVEN policy     IS A `The policy as declared`
      claim      IS A `A claim against an insured`
      d          IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL I — the insuring agreement reaches the claim` policy claim d MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the insured is legally obligated to pay the sums claimed as damages`
    AND `the harm is bodily injury or property damage as defined` policy claim d
    AND `the harm was caused by an occurrence` claim

§§ `Exclusions`
-- src:338 | Exclusions
-- src:340 | This insurance does not apply:

-- src:342 | (a) to liability assumed by the insured under any contract or agreement except an incidental contract; but this exclusion
-- src:343 | does not apply to a warranty of fitness or quality of the named insured's products or a warranty that work performed by
-- src:344 | or on behalf of the named insured will be done in a workmanlike manner;
@ref src:342-344
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (a) applies` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the insured assumed liability for the harm under a contract or agreement`
    AND NOT "except an incidental contract" ... `that contract or agreement is an incidental contract` claim
    AND NOT "but" ... (    `for` claim `,` `the liability is under a warranty of fitness or quality of the named insured's products`
             OR  `for` claim `,` `the liability is under a warranty that work performed by or on behalf of the named insured will be done in a workmanlike manner`)

-- src:346 | (b) to bodily injury or property damage arising out of the ownership, maintenance, operation, use, loading or unloading of
-- src:348 | (1) any automobile or aircraft owned or operated by or rented or loaned to any insured, or
-- src:350 | (2) any other automobile or aircraft operated by any person in the course of his employment by any insured;
-- src:352 | but this exclusion does not apply to the parking of an automobile on premises owned by rented to or controlled by the
-- src:353 | named insured or the ways immediately adjoining, if such automobile is not owned by or rented or loaned to any
-- src:354 | insured;
@ref src:346-354
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the conveyance is owned or operated by, or rented or loaned to, or operated in the course of employment by, an insured` claim MEANS
        "(1)" ... (    `for` claim `,` `the conveyance is owned by an insured`
                   OR  `for` claim `,` `the conveyance is operated by an insured`
                   OR  `for` claim `,` `the conveyance is rented or loaned to an insured`)
    OR  "(2)" ... `for` claim `,` `the conveyance is operated by a person in the course of employment by an insured`

@ref src:352-354
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the parking exception applies` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of the parking of the vehicle on premises owned by, rented to or controlled by the named insured, or the ways immediately adjoining`
    AND `the vehicle is an automobile` claim
    AND NOT `for` claim `,` `the conveyance is owned by an insured`
    AND NOT `for` claim `,` `the conveyance is rented or loaned to an insured`

@ref src:346-354
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (b) applies` claim MEANS
        (   (    `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of the ownership, maintenance, operation, use, loading or unloading of the vehicle`
             AND `the vehicle is an automobile` claim)
         OR `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of the ownership, maintenance, operation, use, loading or unloading of an aircraft`)
    AND `the conveyance is owned or operated by, or rented or loaned to, or operated in the course of employment by, an insured` claim
    AND NOT `the parking exception applies` claim

-- src:356 | (c) to bodily injury or property damage arising out of (1) the ownership maintenance, operation, use, loading or unloading of
-- src:357 | any mobile equipment while being used in any prearranged or organized racing, speed or demolition contest or in any
-- src:358 | stunting activity or in practice or preparation for any such contest or activity or (2) the operation or use of any
-- src:359 | snowmobile or trailer designed for use therewith;
@ref src:356-359
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (c) applies` claim MEANS
        "(1)" ... (    `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of the ownership, maintenance, operation, use, loading or unloading of the vehicle`
                   AND `the vehicle is mobile equipment` claim
                   AND `for` claim `,` `the vehicle was being used in a prearranged or organized racing, speed or demolition contest, in a stunting activity, or in practice or preparation for such a contest or activity`)
    OR  "(2)" ... `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of the operation or use of a snowmobile or a trailer designed for use with one`

-- src:361 | (d) to bodily injury or property damage arising out of and in the course of the transportation of mobile equipment by an
-- src:362 | automobile owned or operated by or rented or loaned to any insured;
@ref src:361-362
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (d) applies` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of and in the course of the transportation of the vehicle by an automobile owned or operated by, or rented or loaned to, an insured`
    AND `the vehicle is mobile equipment` claim

-- src:364 | (e) to bodily injury or property damage arising out of the ownership, maintenance, operation, use, loading or unloading of
-- src:366 | (1) any watercraft owned or operated by or rented or loaned to any insured, or
-- src:368 | (2) any other watercraft operated by any person in the course of his employment by any insured;
-- src:370 | but this exclusion does not apply to watercraft while ashore on premises owned by, rented to or controlled by the named
-- src:371 | insured;
@ref src:364-371
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (e) applies` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of the ownership, maintenance, operation, use, loading or unloading of a watercraft`
    AND `the conveyance is owned or operated by, or rented or loaned to, or operated in the course of employment by, an insured` claim
    AND NOT "but" ... `for` claim `,` `the watercraft was ashore on premises owned by, rented to or controlled by the named insured`

-- src:373 | (f) to bodily injury or property damage arising out of the discharge, dispersal, release or escape of smoke, vapors, soot,
-- src:374 | fumes, acids, alkalis, toxic chemicals, liquids or gases, waste materials or other irritants, contaminants or pollutants into
-- src:375 | or upon land, the atmosphere or any water course or body of water; but this exclusion does not apply if such discharge,
-- src:376 | dispersal, release or escape is sudden and accidental;
@ref src:373-376
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (f) applies` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of the discharge, dispersal, release or escape of smoke, vapors, soot, fumes, acids, alkalis, toxic chemicals, liquids or gases, waste materials or other irritants, contaminants or pollutants into or upon land, the atmosphere or a water course or body of water`
    AND NOT "but" ... `for` claim `,` `that discharge, dispersal, release or escape was sudden and accidental`

-- (g) reaches war only "with respect to" (1) contractual liability under an incidental
-- contract and (2) first aid expenses. (1) is a ground of no cover; (2) takes the first
-- aid expenses out of the sums (msig-cgl-answer.l4). The War and Terrorism Exclusion
-- (Special Conditions) reaches all war loss in any case.
-- src:378 | (g) to bodily injury or property damage due to war, whether or not declared, civil war. insurrection, rebellion or revolution or
-- src:379 | to any act or condition incident to any of the foregoing, with respect to
-- src:381 | (1) liability assumed by the insured under an incidental contract, or
-- src:383 | (2) expenses for first aid under the Supplementary Payments provision;
@ref src:378-381
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (g) applies` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the harm is due to war, whether or not declared, civil war, insurrection, rebellion or revolution, or an act or condition incident to any of them`
    AND "(1)" ... `the insured assumed liability for the harm under an incidental contract` claim

@ref src:378-383
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (g)(2) takes out the first aid expenses` claim MEANS
    `for` claim `,` `the harm is due to war, whether or not declared, civil war, insurrection, rebellion or revolution, or an act or condition incident to any of them`

-- "but part (ii) of this exclusion does not apply with respect to liability ... as an
-- owner or lessor described in (2)": so (1) is excluded under (i) or (ii), and (2) under
-- (i) only.
-- src:385 | (h) to bodily injury or property damage for which the insured or his indemnitee may be held liable
-- src:387 | (1) as a person or organization engaged in the business of manufacturing, distributing, selling or serving alcoholic
-- src:388 | beverages, or
-- src:390 | (2) if not so engaged, as an owner or lessor of premises used for such purposes,
-- src:392 | if such liability is imposed
-- src:394 | (i) by, or because of the violation of, any statute, ordinance of regulation pertaining to the sale, gift, distribution or use
-- src:395 | of any alcoholic beverage, or
-- src:396 | Page 6 of 14
-- src:398 | Revised General Liability Policy Form
-- src:399 | (ii) by reason of the selling, serving or giving of any alcoholic beverage to a minor or to a person under the influence of
-- src:400 | alcohol or which causes or contributes to the intoxication of any person;
-- src:402 | but part (ii) of this exclusion does not apply with respect to liability of the insured or his indemnitee as an owner or lessor
-- src:403 | described in (2) above;
@ref src:385-403
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (h) applies` claim MEANS
        "(1)" ... (    `for` claim `,` `the insured may be held liable as a person or organization engaged in the business of manufacturing, distributing, selling or serving alcoholic beverages`
                   OR  `for` claim `,` `the insured's indemnitee may be held liable as a person or organization engaged in the business of manufacturing, distributing, selling or serving alcoholic beverages`)
              AND (    "(i)" ... `for` claim `,` `the liability is imposed by, or because of the violation of, a statute, ordinance or regulation pertaining to the sale, gift, distribution or use of an alcoholic beverage`
                   OR "(ii)" ... `for` claim `,` `the liability is imposed by reason of selling, serving or giving an alcoholic beverage to a minor or to a person under the influence of alcohol, or which causes or contributes to the intoxication of a person`)
    OR  "(2)" ... (    `for` claim `,` `the insured may be held liable, not being so engaged, as an owner or lessor of premises used for such purposes`
                   OR  `for` claim `,` `the insured's indemnitee may be held liable, not being so engaged, as an owner or lessor of premises used for such purposes`)
              AND "(i)" ... `for` claim `,` `the liability is imposed by, or because of the violation of, a statute, ordinance or regulation pertaining to the sale, gift, distribution or use of an alcoholic beverage`

-- src:405 | (i) to any obligation for which the insured or any carrier as his insurer may be held liable under any workmen's
-- src:406 | compensation, unemployment compensation or disability benefits law, or under any similar law;
@ref src:405-406
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (i) applies` claim MEANS
    `for` claim `,` `the claim is for an obligation for which the insured or a carrier as its insurer may be held liable under a workmen's compensation, unemployment compensation or disability benefits law, or a similar law`

-- src:408 | (j) to bodily injury to any employee of the insured arising out of and in the course of his employment by the insured or to
-- src:409 | any obligation of the insured to indemnify another because of damages arising out of such injury; but this exclusion does
-- src:410 | not apply to liability assumed by the insured under an incidental contract;
@ref src:408-410
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (j) applies` claim MEANS
        `the harm is bodily injury` claim
    AND `for` claim `,` `the bodily injury is to an employee of the insured, arising out of and in the course of employment by the insured`
    AND NOT "but" ... `the insured assumed liability for the harm under an incidental contract` claim

-- src:412 | (k) to property damage to
-- src:414 | (1) property owned or occupied by or rented to the insured,
-- src:416 | (2) property used by the insured, or
-- src:418 | (3) property in the care, custody or control of the insured or as to which the insured is for any purpose exercising
-- src:419 | physical control;
-- src:421 | but parts (2) and (3) of this exclusion do not apply with respect to liability under a written sidetrack agreement and part
-- src:422 | (3) of this exclusion does not apply with respect to property damage (other than to elevator) arising out of the use of an
-- src:423 | elevator at premises owned by, rented to or controlled by the named insured;
@ref src:421
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liability is under a written sidetrack agreement` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the insured assumed liability for the harm under a contract or agreement`
    AND `for` claim `,` `that contract or agreement is in writing`
    AND `for` claim `,` `that contract or agreement is a sidetrack agreement`

@ref src:422-423
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the elevator exception to part (3) applies` claim MEANS
        `the device is an elevator` claim
    AND `for` claim `,` `the property damage arises out of the use of the device at premises owned by, rented to or controlled by the named insured`
    AND NOT "(other than to elevator)" ... `for` claim `,` `the damaged property is the device`

@ref src:412-423
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (k) applies` claim MEANS
        `the harm is property damage` claim
    AND (   "(1)" ... `for` claim `,` `the damaged property is owned or occupied by, or rented to, the insured`
         OR "(2)" ... (    `for` claim `,` `the damaged property is used by the insured`
                       AND NOT `the liability is under a written sidetrack agreement` claim)
         OR "(3)" ... (    `for` claim `,` `the damaged property is in the care, custody or control of the insured, or the insured is for any purpose exercising physical control over it`
                       AND NOT `the liability is under a written sidetrack agreement` claim
                       AND NOT `the elevator exception to part (3) applies` claim))

-- src:425 | (I) to property damage to premises alienated by the named insured arising out of such premises or any part thereof;
@ref src:425
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (l) applies` claim MEANS
        `the harm is property damage` claim
    AND `for` claim `,` `the damaged property is premises alienated by the named insured`
    AND `for` claim `,` `the property damage arises out of those premises or any part of them`

-- src:427 | (m) to loss of use of tangible property which has not been physically injured or destroyed resulting from
-- src:429 | (1) a delay in or lack of performance by or on behalf of the named insured of any contract or agreement, or
-- src:431 | (2) the failure of the named insured's products or work performed by or on behalf of the named insured to meet the
-- src:432 | level of performance, quality, fitness or durability warranted or represented by the named insured;
-- src:434 | but this exclusion does not apply to loss of use of other tangible property resulting from the sudden and accidental
-- src:435 | physical injury to or destruction of the named insured's products or work performed by or on behalf of the named
-- src:436 | insured after such products or work have been put to use by any person or organization other than an insured;
@ref src:427-436
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (m) applies` claim MEANS
        claim's `the harm` EQUALS `loss of use of tangible property which has not been physically injured or destroyed`
    AND (   "(1)" ... `for` claim `,` `the loss of use results from a delay in or lack of performance by or on behalf of the named insured of a contract or agreement`
         OR "(2)" ... `for` claim `,` `the loss of use results from the failure of the named insured's products or work performed by or on behalf of the named insured to meet the level of performance, quality, fitness or durability warranted or represented by the named insured`)
    AND NOT "but" ... `for` claim `,` `the loss of use results from sudden and accidental physical injury to or destruction of the named insured's products or work performed by or on behalf of the named insured, after they had been put to use by a person or organization other than an insured`

-- src:438 | (n) to property damage to the named insured's products arising out of such products or any part of such products;
@ref src:438
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (n) applies` claim MEANS
        `the harm is property damage` claim
    AND `for` claim `,` `the damaged property is the named insured's products`
    AND `for` claim `,` `the property damage arises out of those products or any part of them`

-- src:440 | (o) to property damage to work performed by or on behalf of the named insured arising out of the work or any portion
-- src:441 | thereof, or out of materials, parts or equipment furnished in connection therewith;
@ref src:440-441
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (o) applies` claim MEANS
        `the harm is property damage` claim
    AND `for` claim `,` `the damaged property is work performed by or on behalf of the named insured`
    AND `for` claim `,` `the property damage arises out of that work or any portion of it, or out of materials, parts or equipment furnished in connection with it`

-- src:443 | (p) to damages claimed for the withdrawal, inspection, repair, replacement, or loss of use of the named insured's products
-- src:444 | or work completed by or for the named insured or of any property of which such products or work form a part, if such
-- src:445 | products, work or property are withdrawn from the market or from use because of any known or suspected defect or
-- src:446 | deficiency therein;
@ref src:443-446
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (p) applies` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the damages are claimed for the withdrawal, inspection, repair, replacement or loss of use of the named insured's products or work completed by or for the named insured, or of property of which they form a part`
    AND `for` claim `,` `those products, that work or that property were withdrawn from the market or from use because of a known or suspected defect or deficiency in them`

-- src:448 | (q) to property damage included within:
-- src:450 | (1) the explosion hazard in connection with operations identified in this Policy by a classification code number which
-- src:451 | includes the symbol "x",
-- src:453 | (2) the collapse hazard in connection with operations identified in this Policy by a classification code number which
-- src:454 | includes the symbol "c",
-- src:456 | (3) the underground property damage hazard in connection with operations identified in this Policy by a classification
-- src:457 | code number which includes the symbol "u”
@ref src:448-457
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL exclusion (q) applies` claim MEANS
        "(1)" ... (    `the property damage is included within the explosion hazard` claim
                   AND `for` claim `,` `the operations are identified in the Policy by a classification code number which includes the symbol x`)
    OR  "(2)" ... (    `the property damage is included within the collapse hazard` claim
                   AND `for` claim `,` `the operations are identified in the Policy by a classification code number which includes the symbol c`)
    OR  "(3)" ... (    `the property damage is included within the underground property damage hazard` claim
                   AND `for` claim `,` `the operations are identified in the Policy by a classification code number which includes the symbol u`)

§§ `II. PERSONS INSURED`

-- src:460 | II. PERSONS INSURED
-- src:462 | Each of the following is an insured under this insurance to the extent set forth below:
-- (a)-(c) follow the designation of the named insured in the declarations.
-- src:464 | (a) if the named insured is designated in the declarations as an individual, the person so designated but only with respect to
-- src:465 | the conduct of a business of which he is the sole proprietor, and the spouse of the named insured with respect to the
-- src:466 | conduct of such a business.
-- src:468 | (b) if the named insured is designated in the declarations as a partnership or joint venture, the partnership or joint venture so
-- src:469 | designated and any partner or member thereof but only with respect to his liability as such;
-- src:471 | (c) if the named insured is designated in the declarations as other than an individual, partnership or joint venture, the
-- src:472 | organization so designated and any executive officer, director or stockholder thereof while acting within the scope of his
-- src:473 | duties as such;
@ref src:464-473
GIVEN policy IS A `The policy as declared`
      claim  IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Persons Insured (a)-(c) — the named insured or a person of it is an insured` policy claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `the person claimed against`
    WHEN `the named insured` THEN
        CONSIDER policy's `the named insured is designated in the declarations as`
        WHEN `an individual` THEN
            "(a) but only with respect to" ... `for` claim `,` `the claim concerns the conduct of a business of which the named insured is the sole proprietor`
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHEN `the spouse of the named insured` THEN
            "(a)" ... policy's `the named insured is designated in the declarations as` EQUALS `an individual`
        AND `for` claim `,` `the claim concerns the conduct of a business of which the named insured is the sole proprietor`
    WHEN `a partner or member of the named insured` THEN
            "(b)" ... policy's `the named insured is designated in the declarations as` EQUALS `a partnership or joint venture`
        AND `for` claim `,` `the liability is that of the partner or member as such`
    WHEN `an executive officer, director or stockholder of the named insured` THEN
            "(c)" ... policy's `the named insured is designated in the declarations as` EQUALS `an organization other than an individual, partnership or joint venture`
        AND `for` claim `,` `the executive officer, director or stockholder was acting within the scope of their duties as such`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (e) operates only for mobile equipment registered under a motor vehicle registration law
-- and operated on a public highway, and its proviso takes two kinds of harm out.
-- src:475 | (d) any person (other than an employee of the named insured) or organization while acting as real estate manager for the
-- src:476 | Page 7 of 14
-- src:478 | Revised General Liability Policy Form
-- src:479 | named insured; and
-- src:481 | (e) with respect to the operation, for the purpose of locomotion upon a public highway, of mobile equipment registered
-- src:482 | under any motor vehicle registration law,
-- src:484 | (i) an employee of the named insured while operating any such equipment in the course of his employment, and
-- src:486 | (ii) any other person while operating with the permission of the named insured any such equipment registered in the
-- src:487 | name of the named insured and any person or organization legally responsible for such operation, but only if there is
-- src:488 | no other valid and collectible insurance available, either on a primary or excess basis, to such person or
-- src:489 | organization;
-- src:491 | provided that no person or organization shall be an insured under this paragraph (e) with respect to:
-- src:493 | (1) bodily injury to any fellow employee of such person injured in the course of his employment, or
-- src:495 | (2) property damage to property owned by, rented to, in charge of or occupied by the named insured or the employer
-- src:496 | of any person described in subparagraph (ii).
@ref src:491-496
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Persons Insured (e) — the proviso takes the harm out` claim MEANS
        "(1)" ... (    `the harm is bodily injury` claim
                   AND `for` claim `,` `the bodily injury is to a fellow employee of the operator, injured in the course of employment`)
    OR  "(2)" ... (    `the harm is property damage` claim
                   AND `for` claim `,` `the damaged property is owned by, rented to, in charge of or occupied by the named insured or the employer of the operator`)

@ref src:481-497
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Persons Insured (e) — the person is an insured for the operation of mobile equipment` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of the operation, for the purpose of locomotion upon a public highway, of mobile equipment registered under a motor vehicle registration law`
    AND `the person claimed against is one paragraph (e) names` claim
    AND NOT `Persons Insured (e) — the proviso takes the harm out` claim
    WHERE
        `the person claimed against is one paragraph (e) names` c MEANS
            CONSIDER c's `the person claimed against`
            WHEN `an employee of the named insured` THEN
                "(i)" ... `for` c `,` `the employee was operating the mobile equipment in the course of employment`
            WHEN `a person other than an employee of the named insured, operating mobile equipment` THEN
                "(ii)" ... `paragraph (e)(ii) is met` c
            WHEN `a person or organization legally responsible for the operation of mobile equipment` THEN
                "(ii)" ... `paragraph (e)(ii) is met` c
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `paragraph (e)(ii) is met` c MEANS
                `for` c `,` `the person was operating the mobile equipment with the permission of the named insured`
            AND `for` c `,` `the mobile equipment is registered in the name of the named insured`
            AND NOT "but only if" ... `for` c `,` `other valid and collectible insurance is available, on a primary or excess basis, to the person or organization claimed against`

@ref src:462-497, 281-285
GIVEN policy IS A `The policy as declared`
      claim  IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL II — the person claimed against is an insured` policy claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `the person claimed against`
    WHEN `a person who is not an employee of the named insured, or an organization, acting as real estate manager for the named insured` THEN
        "(d)" ... TRUE
    WHEN `an employee of the named insured` THEN
        `Persons Insured (e) — the person is an insured for the operation of mobile equipment` claim
    WHEN `a person other than an employee of the named insured, operating mobile equipment` THEN
        `Persons Insured (e) — the person is an insured for the operation of mobile equipment` claim
    WHEN `a person or organization legally responsible for the operation of mobile equipment` THEN
        `Persons Insured (e) — the person is an insured for the operation of mobile equipment` claim
    WHEN `the legal representative of the named insured, who has died` THEN
        `Condition 8 — on the named insured's death, the person claimed against is an insured` claim
    WHEN `the person having proper temporary custody of the property of the named insured, who has died` THEN
        `Condition 8 — on the named insured's death, the person claimed against is an insured` claim
    OTHERWISE `Persons Insured (a)-(c) — the named insured or a person of it is an insured` policy claim

-- The closing sentence of II stands indented under (e) in the CGL part (src:498) and at
-- the margin in the P&CO part (src:659). It is read as applying to the whole part in
-- both (NOTES.md, fork F7).
-- src:498 | This insurance does not apply to bodily injury or property damage arising out of the conduct of any partnership or joint
-- src:499 | venture of which the insured is a partner or member and which is not designated in this Policy as a named insured.
@ref src:498-499
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL II — the undesignated partnership or joint venture exclusion applies` claim MEANS
    `for` claim `,` `the harm arises out of the conduct of a partnership or joint venture of which the insured is a partner or member and which is not designated in the Policy as a named insured`

§§ `III. LIMITS OF LIABILITY`

-- III as printed: separate bodily injury and property damage limits, each "each
-- occurrence" with an "aggregate" for the classes of harm named. Superseded by the
-- Combined Single Limit Endorsement where the schedule states a combined limit (NOTES.md,
-- fork F10). The one-occurrence rule (src:542-544) is in msig-cgl-definitions.l4.
-- src:502 | III. LIMITS OF LIABILITY
-- src:504 | Regardless of the number of (1) insureds under this Policy, (2) persons or organizations who sustain bodily injury or property
-- src:505 | damage, or (3) claims made or suits brought on account of bodily injury or property damage, the Company's liability is
-- src:506 | limited as follows:
-- src:508 | Coverage A - The total liability of the Company for all damages, including damages for care and loss of services, because
-- src:509 | of bodily injury sustained by one or more persons as the result of any one occurrence shall not exceed the limit of bodily
-- src:510 | injury liability stated in the schedule as applicable to "each occurrence".
-- src:512 | Subject to the above provision respecting "each occurrence", the total liability of the Company for all damages because of (1)
-- src:513 | all bodily injury included within the completed operations hazard and (2) all bodily injury included within the products hazard
-- src:514 | shall not exceed the limit of bodily injury liability stated in the schedule as "aggregate".
@ref src:512-514
-- Each aggregate predicate asks whether the OCCURRENCE (through the claim that stands for
-- it) falls in the class the aggregate names; the coverage (A for bodily injury, B for
-- property damage) is applied to the damages by msig-cgl-answer.l4.
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL III Coverage A — the occurrence falls under the bodily injury aggregate` claim MEANS
        "(1)" ... `the harm is included within the completed operations hazard` claim
    OR  "(2)" ... `the harm is included within the products hazard` claim

-- src:516 | Coverage B - The total liability of the Company for all damages because of all property damage sustained by one or more
-- src:517 | persons or organizations as the result of any one occurrence shall not exceed the limit of property damage liability stated in
-- src:518 | the schedule as applicable to "each occurrence".
-- src:520 | Subject to the above provision respecting "each occurrence", the total liability of the Company for all damages because of
-- src:521 | all property damage to which this coverage applies and described in any of the numbered subparagraphs below shall not
-- src:522 | exceed the limit of property damage liability stated in the schedule as "aggregate";
-- src:524 | (1) all property damage arising out of premises or operations rated on a remuneration basis or contractor's equipment
-- src:525 | rated on a receipts basis, including property damage for which liability is assumed under any incidental contract relating
-- src:526 | to such premises or operations, but excluding property damage included in subparagraph (2) below;
-- src:528 | (2) all property damage arising out of and occurring in the course of operations performed for the named insured by
-- src:529 | independent contractors and general supervision thereof by the named insured, including any such property damage
-- src:530 | for which liability is assumed under any incidental contract relating to such operations, but this subparagraph (2) does
-- src:531 | not include property damage arising out of maintenance or repairs at premises owned by or rented to the named
-- src:532 | insured or structural alterations at such premises which do not involve changing the size of or moving buildings or other
-- src:533 | structures;
-- src:535 | (3) all property damage included within the products hazard and all property damage included within the completed
-- src:536 | operations hazard.
-- src:538 | Such aggregate limit shall apply separately to the property damage described in subparagraphs (1), (2) and (3) above, and
-- src:539 | under subparagraphs (1) and (2), separately with respect to each project away from premises owned by or rented to the
-- src:540 | named insured.
@ref src:520-536
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL III Coverage B — the occurrence falls under a property damage aggregate` claim MEANS
        "(1)" ... (    `for` claim `,` `the property damage arises out of premises or operations rated on a remuneration basis, or contractor's equipment rated on a receipts basis`
                   AND NOT `the property damage is within subparagraph (2)` claim)
    ..  "(2)" ... `the property damage is within subparagraph (2)` claim
    OR  "(3)" ... (    `the harm is included within the products hazard` claim
                   OR  `the harm is included within the completed operations hazard` claim)
    WHERE
        `the property damage is within subparagraph (2)` c MEANS
                `for` c `,` `the property damage arises out of and occurs in the course of operations performed for the named insured by independent contractors and general supervision thereof by the named insured`
            AND NOT `for` c `,` `the property damage arises out of maintenance or repairs at premises owned by or rented to the named insured, or structural alterations there which do not involve changing the size of or moving buildings or other structures`

-- The cap III puts on what the Company pays for the occurrence, under each coverage:
-- "each occurrence", and, where an aggregate applies, what is left of it.
@ref src:508-540
GIVEN `each occurrence` IS A NUMBER
      aggregate         IS A NUMBER
      `already paid`    IS A NUMBER
      `aggregate applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cap of` `each occurrence` `each occurrence, and of` aggregate `aggregate less` `already paid` `if it applies:` `aggregate applies` MEANS
    IF   `aggregate applies`
    THEN min `each occurrence` (max 0 (aggregate MINUS `already paid`))
    ELSE `each occurrence`

§§ `IV. POLICY TERRITORY`

-- src:547 | IV. POLICY TERRITORY
-- src:549 | This insurance applies only to bodily injury or property damage which occurs within the policy territory.
@ref src:549
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`CGL IV — the harm occurs within the policy territory` claim MEANS
    `the harm occurs within the policy territory` claim
